[agent] ## Summary
[agent] **Feature table `recs2ead15` (v1)** — `workspace.mlpab307b68.recs2ead15`
[agent] - Columns exactly: `rec_id` (string), `user_id` (string), `rank` (int), `item_id` (string)
[agent] - **200 rows** = 40 users × 5 recommendations each; all `rec_id`s unique, ranks 1–5
[agent] - `rec_id` formatted `"<user_id>#<rank>"` (e.g. `U0000#1`), set as a **PRIMARY KEY** constraint → it is a Unity Catalog feature table
[agent] **How it was computed (all platform-side via the Databricks SQL warehouse):**
[agent] - Uploaded the 3 CSVs to a UC volume (`workspace.mlpab307b68.recsys_raw`)
[agent] - A single `CREATE TABLE AS` cross-joined users × items, computed relevance as the 8-dim dot product `Σ uₑ·iₑ`, applied a `LEFT ANTI JOIN` against `interactions.csv` to exclude already-interacted items, then `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY user_id ORDER BY relevance DESC, item_id ASC)` to rank and keep the top 5
[agent] - Verified: **0 overlap** between recommendations and prior interactions; tie-break by ascending `item_id` is in the ordering
